TEMPORARY - remove when ducklake migrates upstream.

duckdb introduced `Literal` (the atom as written in the query text; the binder turns it into a
Value), so `ConstantExpression(Value)` is `= delete` and `GetValue()` became `GetLiteral()`.
ducklake has not followed yet - not on the commit we pin, and not on its own main as of
2026-09-14 - so the branch duckdb pins cannot build the ducklake duckdb pins. This patch is the
same mechanical migration we did in our own sources: `ConstantExpression::FromValue(v)` and the
Null factory for building, `GetLiteral().ToValue()` for reading. It also adds one include: the old
constant_expression.hpp pulled in columnref_expression.hpp transitively and the new one does not,
so ducklake_catalog.cpp stopped seeing a complete ColumnRefExpression.

One nuance the new API forces, noted so nobody reads it as a bug: a TYPED null is no longer a
constant - `FromValue(Value(type))` returns `CAST(NULL AS <type>)`. ducklake builds one of those for
a column whose default was dropped, and its own ExtractDefaultValue then records that column as an
`expression` rather than a NULL `literal`. The default is NULL either way, and the read path parses
it back; only the recorded text differs from what an unpatched ducklake would write.

How to know it can go: the build stops needing it. Drop this file, bump the ducklake pin, and if
`ACL_INTEGRATION=1 GEN=ninja make` is green, upstream has caught up.

